# Keep JavaScript on LF in the repo AND in the worktree.
#
# Several tests slice extension sources between multi-line anchors; a CRLF
# worktree (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) made those anchors miss and turned
# three suites red for reasons that had nothing to do with the code — one as a
# false assertion failure, two as a throw that took the whole file down.
# Git already stored LF — this stops the checkout from converting it back.
#
# One line per extension: git's pathspec here is fnmatch, NOT a shell glob, so
# a braced *.{js,mjs,cjs} would match nothing at all and fail silently.
*.js  text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
